  "implementation": [
    "Only operation-bearing correlated session.cancel enters command dispatch. All other correlated observations still require exact scoped waiters. Signature, replay, named scope and actual host authority are unchanged; the held-command step-up path applies to this closed command exception.",
    "Verified caller CID/SID/request and exact PeerAdmission metadata are registered synchronously before invitation ACK, under the existing source command fence. Background workers cannot overwrite a newer reference. Metadata has a60s bound and the original physical lifetime; no idle source reader is retained.",
    "Current correlated cancellation checks that metadata and then uses the same ordinary Session-control transaction and logical receipt as other cancellation commands. The physical reference is an assertion, not logical identity or a new authorization grant.",
    "A sealed same-physical admission comparison supports current credential rotation/step-up without using a stale route as authority. Actual decision delivery still requires a current route and fresh source reader."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "23 of61 assigned clauses now locally qualified;38 remain. G6-046 and all105 tasks remain in scope.",
    "References are process-local bounded metadata. Restart/reconnect or expiry requires logical invitation replay for a new reference; no old physical wire ID is revived.",
    "Recipient notification is a bounded hint; the authoritative journal/snapshot supplies recovery. Full0081 Session lifecycle, immediate codec replacement0111, handle allocation0109 and broader profiles remain open.",
    "No Linux, production remote/browser/provider, named G6-093 qualification, acceptance or publication."
  ],
